OL,3,GNEWSAReopening line 'a no-brainer' or
OL,4,A'insanely expensive'?
OL,5,
OL,6,FSupporters of a bid to re-open a
OL,7,Frailway line closed for more than 50
OL,8,Fyears say their campaign "never had a
OL,9,Fbetter opportunity" to succeed.
OL,11,FThe Skipton East Lancashire Rail Action
OL,12,FPartnership (SELRAP) has launched a new
OL,13,Fpetition calling on the government to
OL,14,Freinstate the 12-mile (19km) Colne to
OL,15,FSkipton line, which has been shut since
OL,16,F1970.
OL,18,FNick Tennant, vice chair of SELRAP
OL,19,Fsaid: "Even the rail minister has said
OL,20,Fit's a good strategic scheme that is
OL,21,Fneeded, and that's echoed across the
OL,22,Fboard. It's a no-brainer."
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,404,400,260,160,0,100
